    "text": "Fandango at Home Rent Plane on Fandango at Home, or buy it on Fandango at Home. Critics Consensus Plane charts a standard action-adventure course with its cruising altitude just a few miles above Direct-to-Video -- but with Gerard Butler in the cockpit, thriller enthusiasts will still find this a fun flight. Read Critics Reviews Audience Says Check your critical thinking at the gate: The plot's preposterous and loaded with entertaining action, making Plane plenty of good old-fashioned fun. Read Audience Reviews Clarisse Loughrey Independent (UK) 01/31/2023 But Plane is stifled by just how ordinary it is, and how closely it hews to the standard tropes of action films with longer, more descriptive -- yet less ridiculous -- titles. Go to Full Review Kevin Maher The Times (UK) 01/31/2023 Even by Butler’s B-list standards, this is borderline inept. Go to Full Review Plane: Movie Clip - Don't Talk, Just Listen Plane: Movie Clip - Don't Talk, Just Listen 0:46 Plane: Movie Clip - I'm in Charge Plane: Movie Clip - I'm in Charge 1:05 No Way Up 36% No Way Up Watchlist TRAILER for No Way Up Triple Frontier 71% 58% Triple Frontier Watchlist TRAILER for Triple Frontier Mechanic: Resurrection 30% 40% Mechanic: Resurrection Watchlist TRAILER for Mechanic: Resurrection The Expendables 2 68% 67% The Expendables 2 Watchlist Plane: Featurette - One Take Fight Scene Plane: Featurette - One Take Fight Scene 2:03 Plane: Final Trailer Plane: Final Trailer 1:00 Synopsis In the white-knuckle action movie PLANE, pilot Brodie Torrance (Gerard Butler) saves his passengers from a lightning strike by making a risky landing on a war-torn island -- only to find that surviving the landing was just the beginning. When most of the passengers are taken hostage by dangerous rebels, the only person Torrance can count on for help is Louis Gaspare (Mike Colter), an accused murderer who was being transported by the FBI. In order to rescue the passengers, Torrance will need Gaspare's help, and will learn there's more to Gaspare than meets the eye. Director Jean-François Richet Producer Lorenzo di Bonaventura, Mark Vahradian, Marc Butan, Gerard Butler, Alan Siegel, Jason Constantine, Eda Kowan, Ara Keshishian Screenwriter Charles Cumming, J.P. Davis Distributor Lionsgate Production Co Olive Hill Media, Di Bonaventura Pictures, G-BASE, MadRiver Pictures, The Searchers NV Rating R (Violence and Language) Genre Action, Adventure, Mystery & Thriller Original Language English Release Date (Theaters) Jan 13, 2023, Wide Release Date (Streaming) Feb 2, 2023 Box Office (Gross USA) $32.1M Runtime 1h 47m Aspect Ratio Scope (2.35:1)",
